There are two ways to get a functional uboot for the socfpga. 
This first is using Altera's uboot git repo and the second is 
combining the auto-generated files from Quartus and adding those 
to an older uboot version. (I apologize I don't have the versions of 
uboot at the moment)
For the second option, the Altera tool flow outputs a set of files 
which are added to a stock uboot version.  Those files capture the 
settings from the Quartus project for your socfpga.  There probably is 
a good chance that Yocto is patching the uboot using some 
default exported configuration files.
We've seen that the git repo usually is more up to date then the 
auto-generated Quartus files since those track a tool release cycle.

